"# Theming and tokens\n\nAll of Nodus's appearance goes through CSS variables (\"tokens\"). Overriding them is enough to dress\nthe library in a brand's colours, in light and dark mode, without touching its CSS.\n\n## 1. Three levels of tokens\n\n| Level | Examples | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Primitives** | `--blue-600`, `--space-4`, `--radius-lg`, `--shadow-md` | The raw palette. Does not change with the theme. |\n| **Semantic** | `--color-primary`, `--color-bg`, `--color-border`, `--radius` | The meaning. Their value changes between light and dark. |\n| **Component** | `--btn-radius`, `--dialog-radius`, `--table-cell-py` | A setting of a single component, derived from a semantic token. |\n\nRule of thumb: **theme at the semantic level**, adjust one specific component at the component\nlevel, and never redefine a primitive. The full list, with the values of the current theme, is on\nthe [All tokens](#/foundations/tokens) page; each component page lists its own tokens.\n\n## 2. Light, dark, and forced theme\n\nOut of the box, Nodus follows the system preference (`prefers-color-scheme`). An attribute on\n`<html>` forces a theme:\n\n```html\n<html data-theme=\"dark\">   <!-- or \"light\"; no attribute: system preference -->\n```\n\nThe dark theme is therefore defined in **two places**: the media query (no attribute set) and\n`[data-theme=\"dark\"]` (forced theme). A dark override must target both.\n\n## 3. Dressing Nodus in a brand's colours\n\nAn application's CSS sits outside Nodus's layers (`@layer`): it always wins, without\n`!important`. Redefine only what changes:\n\n```css\n/* app.css — loaded after nodus.css */\n:root {\n  --color-primary:       var(--violet-500);\n  --color-primary-hover: var(--violet-600);\n  --color-primary-muted: var(--violet-100);\n  --radius:              var(--radius-lg);   /* control radius: buttons, fields, OTP slots */\n}\n\n/* Dark: system preference… */\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n  :root:not([data-theme]) {\n    --color-primary:       var(--violet-400);\n    --color-primary-hover: var(--violet-300);\n    --color-primary-muted: var(--violet-900);\n  --color-primary-muted: var(--violet-900);\n    --color-primary-fg:    var(--zinc-950);\n  }\n}\n/* …and forced theme: same values. */\n[data-theme=\"dark\"] {\n  --color-primary:       var(--violet-400);\n  --color-primary-hover: var(--violet-300);\n  --color-primary-muted: var(--violet-900);\n  --color-primary-fg:    var(--zinc-950);\n}\n```\n\nThree things to know:\n\n- **`--color-primary-solid`** is the solid fill that carries a label (primary button, badge). In\n  light and dark mode alike it follows `--color-primary`; Nodus's dark theme lightens the accent\n  and switches its label to dark (`--color-primary-fg`). If your dark accent must keep a white\n  label, redefine `--color-primary-solid` to a step darker than the accent.\n- **Some tokens come in pairs**: changing `--color-primary` calls for `--color-primary-fg` (the\n  label on top of it), a status colour calls for its `--color-*-on-muted`. The full table:\n  [tokens to redefine together](../../../SPECS.md#jetons-à-redéfinir-ensemble).\n- **Check the contrast.** Nodus's contrast guarantees cover its default values. After an\n  override, the [Colours and surfaces](#/foundations/colors) page shows the contrast measured in\n  the current theme.\n\n## 4. Tuning one component\n\nComponent tokens apply like any CSS variable: on `:root` for the whole application, or on a\ncontainer for one area only.\n\n```css\n:root           { --dialog-radius: var(--radius-xl); --tooltip-font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.admin-zone     { --table-cell-py: var(--space-2); }   /* tighter tables here only */\n#cart-drawer    { --drawer-width: 100vw; }\n```\n\nEvery token listed in the **Tokens** section of a component page really acts on that component:\nthe build checks it.\n\n## 5. Compact density\n\n`data-density=\"compact\"`, on `<html>` or on a container, reduces heights (buttons, fields, menu\nitems, tabs) and spacing (accordion, cards, cells, dialogs). Medium buttons and fields become 28 px\nin 13 px text; headings and body text keep their size.\n\n```html\n<section data-density=\"compact\">…</section>\n```\n\n## 6. What not to do\n\n| Avoid | Why | Instead |\n|---|---|---|\n| Copying all of Nodus's tokens into the application | Frozen values no longer follow updates | Redefine only what changes |\n| Hard-coding a colour (`#fff`, `rgb(…)`) | It does not switch to dark | A semantic token |\n| Reusing a Nodus class (`.timeline { … }`) in the app's CSS | The app's CSS always wins and overrides the component | Prefix your classes, or go through the tokens |\n\nGoing further: [CSS conventions](../../../GUIDELINES.md#4-css--tokens-data--theming) and the\ntoken architecture in [SPECS](../../../SPECS.md).\n"